WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.920
London.

2
00:00:00.970 --> 00:00:03.670
A plain door in a windowless wall.

3
00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:07.870
A man asks his lawyer friend:
"Did you ever remark that door?"

4
00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:11.210
The lawyer, Utterson,
starts collecting papers.

5
00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:12.180
A will.

6
00:00:12.230 --> 00:00:12.630
A letter.

7
00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:15.940
An envelope marked "not to be opened".

8
00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:18.680
Every folder ends with a question mark.

9
00:00:18.730 --> 00:00:20.880
And the last two stay shut.

10
00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:25.110
So why does the novel keep its
biggest secret until the very end?

11
00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:28.380
In this mission, you'll
map how the story is told:

12
00:00:28.430 --> 00:00:30.320
who narrates, and when.

13
00:00:30.370 --> 00:00:35.160
You'll hear a witness try, and
fail, to describe a man called Hyde.

14
00:00:35.210 --> 00:00:40.120
And you'll track every clue, from a
cheque to a final, written statement.

15
00:00:40.170 --> 00:00:44.750
Your mission: explain why the
secret waits until the last chapter.
